														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2045368">
									

<p>There's some awkward wording in there:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1934 is located in Site-19 behind a locked door specifically labeled as SCP-1934 in Corridor 6 of the seventh floor.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>The office was in the process of being cleaned out when the anomaly was discovered by custodial staff as they attempted to enter the office to remove the remaining items.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>No further information on SCP-1934 can be detected given the technological capabilities of the Foundation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>All sentences that could probably benefit from a rewrite. There might be more, but these jumped out at me.</p>
<p>Also:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Access is restricted outside of testing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Since we can't enter the room, isn't that kind of a given? Even disregarding that, that's still kind of a no-brainer.</p>
<p>Anyway, none of those things bother me too much, because in the end this is some weird shit and I - like Kalinin - can almost taste Marlowe's discomfort as she sees herself mutilated over and over again. Like these entities have the room trapped in a loop and are using it to experiment on human beings. And that note is pure gold.</p>
<p>So that gets this a well-deserved +1.</p>

