<p>If there was an incredibly clear glass, you would be able to interact with it in terms of being able to see it under certain circumstances, or see light reflect off of it, or have your fingertips smush against the surface. If you somehow were able to use echolocation<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-344088-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-344088-1')">1</a></sup>, you would detect a solid surface. Simply being transparent doesn't mean the glass isn't there; it's basically detectable and interactive with all senses save for sight.</p>
<p>In the case of SCP-1934, there is none of that.</p>
