<p>Conceptually I agree with you&#8212;-I wanted it to just be the &quot;suddenly it's gone even though it's still there&quot; but no one liked it. The rest of the stuff I didn't just shit out but put in deliberately, making use of concepts I had for something called &quot;Limited-use Door&quot;, so basically I got to merge the two together and I rather prefer it like that.</p>
<p>You must've misunderstood too; there are no 'tenants', that's just the word being used by the figures indicating a severe lack of English comprehension, or a very poor attempt at translation/deception. They were basically referring to the office itself as a &quot;tenement&quot;, based on how much time Marlowe spent in the room previously.</p>
